Package: MimeSys
Title: Template-Based Simulation of Multi-Omics Data
Version: 0.99.0
Date: 2026-10-16
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nalin", "Arora", email = "naa4050@med.cornell.edu",
        role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Himel", "Mallick", email = "himel.mallick@merck.com",
        role = "aut"))
Description: MimeSys simulates realistic multi-omics datasets from a template
    fitted to real data. The template learns each feature's empirical marginal
    distribution, within-view dependence through a low-rank Gaussian copula
    factor model, and cross-view dependence through a shared latent space
    estimated by generalized canonical correlation analysis. Simulated
    datasets can vary sample size, feature counts and the strength of
    cross-view dependence, and can carry controlled signal for continuous,
    binary or survival outcomes, including linear, nonlinear, shared-latent
    and cross-view interaction scenarios, and can simulate mediation with an
    exposure, parallel or sequential mediators in any views, and calibrated
    true direct, indirect and path-specific effects. Inputs and outputs use
    MultiAssayExperiment containers, and diagnostics compare simulated and
    empirical correlation structure and marginal distributions.
